Rules-kind, byte and flight checks, and the field selects no read authority.\n\nThe planner's criteria. The witness compares the hosted card list and resource bytes with the stdio-composed service for the same room, in both cohorts. It shows Claude's hashed domain and ChatGPT's own origin on the same endpoint, and no domain on stdio. A host without UI receives no view_read or view_act tool and no UI metadata.\n\nGates and CI. The gate at a612368f reads exit 0, with matching before and after source guards and a clean status. The terminal shows Node 132, counting 56, plain 3,579 passes with one skip and Native 1,039 passes with two skips. Card run 41472303998 concluded success at a612368f.\n\nEvidence. The manifest hashes to e2c1135f…cc22, as the request states. All 114 files in its five units match their sizes and digests. No unit holds an unlisted or writable file, and each unit's SHA256SUMS matches the manifest and the note's table. The scan for private keys, GitHub tokens and bearer values finds no match. The five named controls each fail their expected assertion and restore source. The first URL control stays recorded as inconclusive, with its reason.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One composition function serves both transports, the native installation decides the cards, and presentation policy stays outside authority.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. The origin setting fails closed, card names cannot reach the omitted tools, and every act stays under the agent's own key.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One item for a later touch. fromInstalledApplication returns the plain service on every failure without saying why. A stdio user whose trust or Git source is wrong sees no cards and no reason. A single stderr line on stdio, or a health field on the hosted agent, would make that diagnosable.\n\nOpen choice. The selection lasts for one HTTP layer, so a reinstall shows new cards only after a bearer rotation or an object restart. Card reads still refuse the retired 